Data sources (P1/S8 INotifyPropertyChanged VM → generated C# client, web hook name kept at the C# call site):
  useAnomalies -> AnomaliesClientFeed.FetchAsync, ApiRequest("get_api_v1_analytics_anomalies",
                  Query{ vehicle_id, days }) — GET /analytics/anomalies
                  (operation id = Operations.Analytics.Anomalies; web default days=7 preserved)
  useSelectedVehicle -> the feed is pre-scoped with vehicleId (+ days) at construction (same seam as the sibling
                  RouteEfficiencyClientFeed); the view binds only the resolved snapshot.
Reused W3 component surfaces: TsStatCard (web StatCard), TsGlassPanel, TsBadge, TsBarChart (the native recharts
  BarChart wrapper), TsEmptyState, TsQueryError, TsSkeleton, TsDataFreshness, TsFadeIn, TsDateTime (relative
  timestamp), PageTitle/Subhead/SectionTitle/PanelTitle/Caption/Text typography, DisplayTokens/StatusResources brushes.
Units (P1/S5): the anomaly value/baseline/z_score are per-signal scalar readings with no fixed physical unit (the web
  renders them with fmtNumber, no unit conversion); the projection rounds at the display boundary only
  (NumberFormatting.Format with the active UnitPref locale). No non-SI value is stored or computed.
Live data: none (web page uses a TanStack-Query read, no useLiveX/SSE), so no SSE subscription / staleness chip
  beyond the standard TsDataFreshness header (ADR-013 live path n/a).
Scope note: the web page also mounts <AIAnomalyExplanations/> and <AILearnedAnomalyBaselines/> — AI-gated,
  withAiFeature-wrapped surfaces that render only when ai_mode != 'off'. Those are their own shipped parity units
  (components/ai/*) and are NOT among this page's 27 manifest parity items (data sources = only useAnomalies;
  panels = 7; charts = 1), so they are out of scope here and intentionally not re-embedded — mirroring how
  RouteEfficiencyPage delegated <AIRouteEfficiencySuggestions/> rather than re-owning it.

